From: sunrisepeak <speakshen@163.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:34:00 +0900
Subject: [clangd] Consumers bind to published prerequisite generations

A consumer binds to the generations of the prerequisites actually published, a freshly published owned build is reported as built, and each producer snapshot covers only its own dependency closure, so an unrelated module change does not rebuild its importers.

* fix(clangd): consumers bind to published prerequisite generations

* [clangd] Report freshly published owned module builds

* perf(modules): each producer binds only its dependency closure

  The build-wave snapshot contained unrelated completed module roots, and every producer key included all of them. Shared importing Base acquired different cache generations when a consumer additionally imported or edited Noise. Preserve the planner dependency closure per node and select immutable prerequisite snapshots from that closure, conservatively retaining unknown prebuilt leaves. Actual transitive dependency changes still invalidate and rebuild consumers.

  The old implementation fails the two unrelated-root reuse assertions. All 77 prerequisite-module controls pass with the change. A private same-recipe original UP20 replay has zero prerequisite/admission failures, 85 actual builds instead of 526, and restores all sources with normal cleanup. The replay is correctness-only, not release or a latency distribution.
